Package: linscp
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: xdg-utils
Description: graphical and console file transfer client for Linux, Windows and Android
 LinSCP is a noncommercial file transfer client inspired by the upstream Windows
 client. It provides an interactive command-line client (linscp) and a dual-pane
 Commander graphical client: natively via Tauri v2 (Linux/WebKitGTK, Windows/WebView2,
 Android/WebView) and in any browser via linscp --serve-http (linscp-gui).
 .
 The desktop entry starts the graphical client through xdg-utils, so
 the browser window is asked for the way a Wayland session expects; without
 xdg-utils the address is printed and nothing is opened.
 .
 SSH, SFTP and SCP are served by pure-Rust crates (russh, russh-sftp) - the
 SFTP v3 wire protocol (with copy-data and check-file-name extensions) and,
 for SCP, the remote-shell directory engine and the rcp transfer protocol;
 FTP/FTPS via suppaftp (async-rustls), WebDAV and S3 via reqwest/rustls with
 custom SPKI pinning and TLS version enforcement. The client provides transfer
 resume and recursive synchronization, public-key, ssh-agent and password
 authentication, host-key verification, stored sessions and a subset of the
 upstream scripting language.
 Protocol support depends on the backend; WebDAV and Amazon S3 support are
 incomplete, and an SCP transfer cannot be resumed, because the rcp
 protocol has no offset to continue from. Full upstream feature parity is
 not provided.
